TC-06 manual evidence — Smart-equipment claim, sharing and clearance
Date: 2026-09-17

Administrator: phase2.manual-admin@fithub.test
Route: /simulation/equipment
Machine: EQ-TREADMILL-01 mapped to persisted TREAD-001 (Treadmill)
Members: Elena Martinez, Priya Testmember, and a third active development Member

Observed successful workflow:
- Connected Mode reported API connected and EquipmentHub connected.
- Four virtual machines mapped to persisted equipment records.
- Eight development Members loaded.
- Elena entered, took her session NFC card and claimed Treadmill.
- Persisted state became Occupied with Elena as owner.
- Elena enabled sharing; persisted state became SharingAllowed.
- Priya joined as the one sharing partner.
- A third Member was rejected with SHARING_FULL.
- Administrator equipment history displayed claim, sharing enabled and partner joined events.
- Connected reset restored TREAD-001 to Available in PostgreSQL.

Failed clearance workflow:
- One shared Member leaving did not initially start clearance, as expected.
- When the second Member left, the event history emitted SENSOR_ZONE_EXITED and CLEARANCE_COUNTDOWN_STARTED, followed by BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE, SENSOR_ZONE_ENTERED and CLEARANCE_COUNTDOWN_CANCELLED in the same transition window.
- The machine remained SharingAllowed; a stable 30-second automatic release could not be demonstrated.
- Similar duplicate enter/start/cancel events were visible in the same event history.

Decision: FAIL
Reason: FR-21 and most of FR-22 were demonstrated, but FR-23 did not complete reliably and FR-24 produced contradictory connected events.
Defect: DEF-004 open.
